# pre-commit — runs automatically when you `git commit`, before the commit is
# created. We use it to lint + format only the files you actually staged, so
# broken or unformatted code never enters a commit. `lint-staged` (configured
# in package.json) runs `eslint --fix` then `prettier --write` on staged *.ts
# files and re-stages them. If eslint finds an error it cannot auto-fix, it
# exits non-zero and the commit is aborted.
#
# Runs first, before lint-staged: scripts/scan-for-obfuscation.mjs checks
# every tracked file for the exact obfuscated-payload signatures confirmed in
# the 2026-09-11 incident (see docs/RAIQUID_CONTEXT.md). No dependencies, no
# install needed, so it can't be skipped by a broken node_modules.
node scripts/scan-for-obfuscation.mjs
npx lint-staged
